WEBVTT

00:00:22.124 --> 00:00:23.952
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.210
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:27.051 --> 00:00:27.687
Mary!

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:28.481
No!

00:00:30.433 --> 00:00:31.452
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:32.684 --> 00:00:34.075
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:36.145 --> 00:00:37.557
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:38.249 --> 00:00:39.383
I can't do this alone.

00:00:41.847 --> 00:00:42.788
No!

00:00:45.403 --> 00:00:46.510
We got work to do.

00:00:47.229 --> 00:00:49.613
This was dad's single
most valuable possession.

00:00:49.681 --> 00:00:51.825
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:51.963 --> 00:00:53.910
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:53.993 --> 00:00:55.266
You know, saving people,

00:00:55.349 --> 00:00:56.373
Hunting things,

00:00:56.428 --> 00:00:57.342
Family business.

00:00:57.425 --> 00:00:57.840
No.

00:00:57.951 --> 00:00:59.267
I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:00.785
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:01:00.844 --> 00:01:02.228
Sam, You know we're gonna find dad,

00:01:02.256 --> 00:01:02.662
Right?

00:01:04.468 --> 00:01:05.668
Yeah. I know.

00:01:47.455 --> 00:01:48.248
Nervous flyer?

00:01:49.104 --> 00:01:50.397
It's that obvious, huh?

00:01:51.507 --> 00:01:53.775
You know, what are the odds
of dying in a plane crash?

00:01:53.981 --> 00:01:54.749
I mean, what

00:01:54.918 --> 00:01:55.949
20,000 to one?

00:01:59.809 --> 00:02:00.334
Wow.

00:02:01.084 --> 00:02:02.996
That's, uh, really
reassuring. Thank you.

00:02:28.872 --> 00:02:29.359
Thanks.

00:02:30.146 --> 00:02:30.615
Miranda,

00:02:30.784 --> 00:02:31.421
How are you today?

00:02:31.605 --> 00:02:32.842
I'm doing just fine, Chuck.

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:35.616
Welcome aboard.

00:02:36.328 --> 00:02:39.083
15c towards the back of
the plane, on the right.

00:02:42.041 --> 00:02:43.259
Have a nice flight, sir.

00:02:46.102 --> 00:02:47.470
Oh, I'm counting on it.

00:02:52.786 --> 00:02:53.442
Um...

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.647
Uh, 11F,

00:02:56.703 --> 00:02:58.615
That's the middle of the
plane, on... Thank you

00:03:00.823 --> 00:03:01.535
...the left.

00:03:13.529 --> 00:03:14.241
Excuse me.

00:03:15.044 --> 00:03:16.319
Do you know how long we've been up?

00:03:16.431 --> 00:03:18.793
Oh, uh... about 40 minutes.

00:03:19.823 --> 00:03:20.386
Wow.

00:03:20.682 --> 00:03:22.050
Time really does fly, huh?

00:03:25.403 --> 00:03:26.115
Excuse me.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.670
I've got to stretch my legs.

00:03:54.332 --> 00:03:55.661
You, what the hell are you doing?!

00:05:07.793 --> 00:05:08.674
Morning, sunshine.

00:05:10.039 --> 00:05:10.807
What time is it?

00:05:10.957 --> 00:05:12.269
Huh, It's about 5:45.

00:05:12.419 --> 00:05:13.131
In the morning?

00:05:13.206 --> 00:05:13.600
Yep.

00:05:13.806 --> 00:05:14.871
Where does the day go?

00:05:16.933 --> 00:05:18.020
Did you get any sleep last night?

00:05:18.226 --> 00:05:19.575
Yeah, I grabbed a couple hours.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:20.288
You, liar

00:05:21.256 --> 00:05:22.381
'Cause I was up at 3:00,

00:05:23.131 --> 00:05:24.930
And you were watching a
George Foreman infomercial.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:25.808
Hey, what can I say?

00:05:25.864 --> 00:05:26.745
It's riveting tv.

00:05:27.176 --> 00:05:28.563
When was the last time you
got a good night's sleep?

00:05:28.807 --> 00:05:29.388
I don't know,

00:05:29.463 --> 00:05:31.053
A little while, I guess.
It's not a big deal

00:05:31.241 --> 00:05:31.971
Yeah, it is.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:33.864
I appreciate your concern.

00:05:33.902 --> 00:05:35.232
I'm not concerned about you.

00:05:35.251 --> 00:05:37.781
It's your job to keep my ass
alive, so I need you sharp.

00:05:39.198 --> 00:05:40.773
Seriously, are you still
having nightmares about Jess?

00:05:46.264 --> 00:05:46.807
Yeah.

00:05:48.585 --> 00:05:50.272
But it's not just her. It's everything.

00:05:50.703 --> 00:05:52.408
I just forgot, you know? This job.

00:05:53.905 --> 00:05:54.805
Man, it gets to you.

00:05:55.123 --> 00:05:57.129
You can't let it. You can't
bring it home like that.

00:05:58.441 --> 00:05:59.003
So, what?

00:05:59.040 --> 00:05:59.603
All this it...

00:05:59.915 --> 00:06:00.946
Never keeps you up at night?

00:06:02.108 --> 00:06:02.576
Never?

00:06:02.932 --> 00:06:03.645
You're never afraid?

00:06:03.926 --> 00:06:04.807
No, not really.

00:06:13.129 --> 00:06:13.913
That's not fear.

00:06:15.225 --> 00:06:16.125
That is precaution.

00:06:16.706 --> 00:06:17.605
All right, whatever.

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:18.749
I'm too tired to argue.

00:06:27.703 --> 00:06:28.246
Hello?

00:06:28.525 --> 00:06:28.974
Dean,

00:06:29.237 --> 00:06:30.905
It's Jerry Panowski.

00:06:31.886 --> 00:06:33.901
You and your dad helped
me out a couple years back.

00:06:34.985 --> 00:06:35.937
Oh, all right,

00:06:35.981 --> 00:06:38.771
Yeah, up in kittanning,
Pennsylvania, the poltergeist thing.

00:06:39.213 --> 00:06:40.143
It's not back, is it?

00:06:40.342 --> 00:06:40.807
No.

00:06:41.184 --> 00:06:41.715
No.

00:06:42.955 --> 00:06:43.774
Thank god, no.

00:06:45.254 --> 00:06:47.003
But it's something else, and...

00:06:47.512 --> 00:06:48.862
Well, I think it could be a lot worse.

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:50.058
What is it?

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:51.648
Can we talk in person?

00:06:57.427 --> 00:06:59.176
Thanks for making the trip so quick.

00:06:59.281 --> 00:07:01.823
I ought to be doing you guys a
favor, not the other way around.

00:07:02.775 --> 00:07:04.280
Dean and your dad really helped me out.

00:07:04.878 --> 00:07:06.516
Yeah, he told me. It was a poltergeist?

00:07:06.583 --> 00:07:07.225
Poltergeist?

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:08.328
Man, I loved that movie.

00:07:08.372 --> 00:07:10.232
Hey, nobody's talking
to you. Keep walking.

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:13.907
Damn right it was a poltergeist
practically tore our house apart.

00:07:14.903 --> 00:07:15.855
Tell you something

00:07:16.493 --> 00:07:17.799
If it wasn't for you and your dad,

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:19.061
I probably wouldn't be alive.

00:07:21.261 --> 00:07:23.033
Your dad said you were off
at college. Is that right?

00:07:23.652 --> 00:07:24.870
Yeah, I was. I'm...

00:07:25.158 --> 00:07:26.287
Taking some time off.

00:07:26.575 --> 00:07:28.169
Well, he was real proud
of you. I could tell.

00:07:28.612 --> 00:07:29.962
He talked about you all the time.

00:07:31.331 --> 00:07:31.951
He did?

00:07:32.327 --> 00:07:33.323
Yeah, you bet he did.

00:07:33.833 --> 00:07:35.781
Oh, hey, I tried to get
ahold of him, but I couldn't.

00:07:36.334 --> 00:07:37.309
How's he doing, anyway?

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:39.434
He's, um

00:07:40.023 --> 00:07:41.352
Wrapped up in a job right now.

00:07:41.617 --> 00:07:43.145
Well, we're missing the old man.

00:07:43.411 --> 00:07:44.363
We get sam.

00:07:44.518 --> 00:07:45.691
Even trade, huh?

00:07:46.223 --> 00:07:47.684
No, not by a long shot.

00:07:48.304 --> 00:07:49.964
I got something I want you guys to hear.

00:07:51.823 --> 00:07:52.930
I listened to this.

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:53.926
Well,

00:07:54.169 --> 00:07:55.653
It sounded like it was up your alley

00:07:55.919 --> 00:07:57.889
Normally I wouldn't have access to this.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:01.737
It's the cockpit voice recorder
for united britannia flight 2485.

00:08:02.025 --> 00:08:02.933
It was one of ours.

00:08:03.456 --> 00:08:03.905
Mayday

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:27.221
Took off from here,

00:08:27.783 --> 00:08:29.555
Crashed about 200 miles south.

00:08:29.834 --> 00:08:31.945
Now, they're saying mechanical failure.

00:08:32.147 --> 00:08:34.490
Cabin depressurized
somehow. Nobody knows why.

00:08:34.848 --> 00:08:36.145
Over 100 people on board.

00:08:36.931 --> 00:08:38.083
Only seven got out alive.

00:08:39.056 --> 00:08:39.837
Pilot was one.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.380
His name is chuck lambert.
He's a good friend of mine.

00:08:42.962 --> 00:08:43.929
Chuck is, uh...

00:08:45.589 --> 00:08:46.887
Well, he's pretty broken up about it,

00:08:47.708 --> 00:08:48.581
Like it was his fault.

00:08:49.416 --> 00:08:50.223
You don't think it was?

00:08:50.766 --> 00:08:51.614
No, I don't.

00:08:52.334 --> 00:08:52.810
Jerry,

00:08:52.996 --> 00:08:54.836
We're gonna need passenger manifests,

00:08:54.921 --> 00:08:56.390
Hum...a list of survivors.

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:56.907
All right.

00:08:57.026 --> 00:08:57.661
And huh...

00:08:57.741 --> 00:08:59.277
Any way we can take a
look at the wreckage?

00:08:59.958 --> 00:09:01.190
The other stuff is no problem,

00:09:01.243 --> 00:09:02.064
But the wreckage

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:05.803
Fellas, the ntsb has it locked
down in an evidence warehouse.

00:09:06.782 --> 00:09:08.292
No way I've got that kind of clearance.

00:09:10.858 --> 00:09:11.348
No problem.

00:09:16.786 --> 00:09:17.237
Hey

00:09:17.395 --> 00:09:17.859
Hi.

00:09:20.825 --> 00:09:21.831
You've been in there forever.

00:09:23.358 --> 00:09:24.391
You can't rush perfection.

00:09:25.132 --> 00:09:26.245
Homeland security?

00:09:27.423 --> 00:09:28.337
That's pretty illegal,

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:29.118
Even for us.

00:09:29.953 --> 00:09:30.456
Yeah, well,

00:09:30.495 --> 00:09:31.820
It's something new, you know?

00:09:31.833 --> 00:09:33.528
People haven't seen it a thousand times.

00:09:38.337 --> 00:09:39.260
All right, so, what do you got?

00:09:39.479 --> 00:09:40.121
Well,

00:09:40.136 --> 00:09:42.702
There's definitely E.V.P. On
the cockpit voice recorder.

00:09:42.812 --> 00:09:43.156
Yeah?

00:09:43.234 --> 00:09:43.735
Listen.

00:09:51.412 --> 00:09:52.429
"No survivors"?

00:09:53.321 --> 00:09:54.051
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:54.061 --> 00:09:55.532
There were seven survivors.

00:09:56.122 --> 00:09:56.748
Got me.

00:09:58.996 --> 00:10:00.514
So, what are you
thinking? A haunted flight?

00:10:00.959 --> 00:10:02.587
There's a long history of spirits and

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:04.638
Death omens on planes and ships,

00:10:04.685 --> 00:10:05.749
Like phantom travelers.

00:10:05.796 --> 00:10:06.203
Mm-Hmm

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.160
Or remember flight 401?

00:10:08.394 --> 00:10:08.848
Right

00:10:09.068 --> 00:10:09.835
The one that crashed,

00:10:09.882 --> 00:10:11.384
The airline salvaged
some of this parts,*

00:10:11.447 --> 00:10:12.527
Put it in other planes,

00:10:12.836 --> 00:10:15.074
Then the spirit of the pilot and
copilot haunted those flights.

00:10:15.137 --> 00:10:15.481
Right.

00:10:15.544 --> 00:10:16.029
Yep.

00:10:16.984 --> 00:10:18.205
Maybe we got a similar deal.

00:10:18.941 --> 00:10:21.320
All rigth so, survivors which
one do you want to talk to first?

00:10:21.373 --> 00:10:23.094
Third on the list Max Jaffey.

00:10:23.188 --> 00:10:23.767
Why him?

00:10:23.814 --> 00:10:25.020
For one, he's from around here.

00:10:25.072 --> 00:10:25.823
And two,

00:10:26.402 --> 00:10:27.780
If anyone saw anything weird.

00:10:28.421 --> 00:10:28.954
He did.

00:10:30.112 --> 00:10:30.973
What makes you say that?

00:10:31.317 --> 00:10:32.554
Well, I spoke to his mother,

00:10:33.359 --> 00:10:34.706
And she told me where to find him.

00:10:37.447 --> 00:10:38.370
I don't understand.

00:10:38.382 --> 00:10:40.329
I already spoke with homeland security.

00:10:40.681 --> 00:10:41.270
Right.

00:10:41.776 --> 00:10:43.308
Some new information has come up.

00:10:43.544 --> 00:10:45.464
So if you could just
answer a couple questions...

00:10:45.669 --> 00:10:47.016
Just before the plane went down,

00:10:47.707 --> 00:10:50.031
Did you notice anything unusual?

00:10:50.368 --> 00:10:51.092
Like what?

00:10:51.884 --> 00:10:53.113
Strange lights,

00:10:53.787 --> 00:10:55.101
Weird noises, maybe...

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.208
Voices.

00:10:58.128 --> 00:10:58.936
No, nothing.

00:11:00.869 --> 00:11:01.711
Mr. Joffey

00:11:02.671 --> 00:11:03.143
Jaffey.

00:11:03.446 --> 00:11:03.951
Jaffey.

00:11:04.086 --> 00:11:05.231
You checked yourself in here,

00:11:05.349 --> 00:11:05.804
Right?

00:11:07.019 --> 00:11:07.815
Can I ask why?

00:11:08.312 --> 00:11:09.619
I was a little stressed.

00:11:09.639 --> 00:11:11.490
I survived a plane crash.

00:11:13.156 --> 00:11:13.733
And that's

00:11:13.833 --> 00:11:14.629
What terrified you?

00:11:14.669 --> 00:11:15.803
That's what you were afraid of?

00:11:15.902 --> 00:11:18.410
I... I don't want to
talk about this anymore.

00:11:18.589 --> 00:11:20.380
I think maybe you did
see something up there.

00:11:21.415 --> 00:11:22.410
We need to know what.

00:11:23.478 --> 00:11:23.956
No.

00:11:24.095 --> 00:11:25.170
No, I was...

00:11:25.309 --> 00:11:26.065
Delusional

00:11:26.844 --> 00:11:27.800
Seeing things.

00:11:29.105 --> 00:11:30.125
He was seeing things.

00:11:33.676 --> 00:11:34.271
It's okay.

00:11:35.737 --> 00:11:38.664
Then just tell us what you
thought you saw, please.

00:11:43.307 --> 00:11:44.038
There was...

00:11:44.277 --> 00:11:44.849
This...

00:11:45.198 --> 00:11:45.866
Man.

00:11:47.551 --> 00:11:48.441
And, uh,

00:11:48.536 --> 00:11:49.951
He had these...

00:11:51.047 --> 00:11:51.670
Eyes...

00:11:51.765 --> 00:11:52.512
These, uh...

00:11:54.587 --> 00:11:55.795
Black eyes.

00:11:57.607 --> 00:11:59.435
And I saw him

00:12:00.215 --> 00:12:02.377
I thought I saw him...

00:12:06.319 --> 00:12:06.923
What?

00:12:09.214 --> 00:12:11.391
He opened the emergency exit.

00:12:13.586 --> 00:12:14.190
But that's...

00:12:14.238 --> 00:12:15.351
That's impossible,

00:12:15.764 --> 00:12:17.022
Right? I mean, I looked it up.

00:12:17.054 --> 00:12:17.944
There's something like

00:12:18.103 --> 00:12:20.200
Two tons of pressure on that door.

00:12:22.364 --> 00:12:22.936
Yeah...

00:12:23.842 --> 00:12:24.732
This man, huh...

00:12:24.812 --> 00:12:27.307
Did he seem to appear and disappear.

00:12:27.564 --> 00:12:29.948
Rapidly.It would look
something like a mirage.

00:12:31.733 --> 00:12:33.052
What are you, nuts?

00:12:35.293 --> 00:12:36.437
He was a passenger.

00:12:36.469 --> 00:12:38.376
He was sitting right in front of me.

00:12:45.485 --> 00:12:46.645
Say here we are

00:12:46.757 --> 00:12:48.902
George Phelps, seat 20c.

00:12:49.538 --> 00:12:50.047
Hmm.

00:12:51.002 --> 00:12:53.196
Man, I don't care how strong you are.

00:12:55.691 --> 00:12:57.725
Even yoked up on pcp or something,

00:12:58.109 --> 00:13:01.097
No way you can open up an
emergency door during a flight.

00:13:02.069 --> 00:13:03.086
Not if you're human.

00:13:04.437 --> 00:13:06.423
But maybe this guy
George was something else

00:13:06.754 --> 00:13:08.915
Some kind of creature,
maybe, in human form.

00:13:09.344 --> 00:13:11.124
Does that look like a
creature's lair to you?

00:13:19.756 --> 00:13:21.059
This is your late husband?

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:23.523
Yes, that was my george.

00:13:24.344 --> 00:13:25.441
And you said he was a...

00:13:26.299 --> 00:13:27.094
Dentist?

00:13:27.514 --> 00:13:28.097
Mm-Hmm.

00:13:29.374 --> 00:13:31.683
He was headed to a convention in Denver.

00:13:34.547 --> 00:13:36.594
Do you know that he
was petrified to fly?

00:13:40.257 --> 00:13:41.666
For him to go like that...

00:13:44.313 --> 00:13:45.553
How long were you married?

00:13:47.957 --> 00:13:49.159
13 years.

00:13:49.916 --> 00:13:51.118
In all that time,

00:13:52.714 --> 00:13:54.442
Did you ever notice anything...

00:13:54.836 --> 00:13:56.339
Strange about him,

00:13:56.864 --> 00:13:58.479
Anything out of the ordinary?

00:14:01.684 --> 00:14:02.379
Well...

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:06.682
Uh, he had acid reflux,

00:14:06.813 --> 00:14:07.883
If that's what you mean.

00:14:12.017 --> 00:14:13.202
I mean it goes without saying.

00:14:13.221 --> 00:14:14.635
It just doesn't make any sense.

00:14:15.037 --> 00:14:16.652
A middle-Aged dentist with an ulcer

00:14:16.671 --> 00:14:18.399
Is not exactly evil personified.

00:14:19.169 --> 00:14:21.310
You know what we need to do is
get inside that ntsb warehouse,

00:14:21.328 --> 00:14:22.812
Check out the wreckage.

00:14:24.654 --> 00:14:25.555
Okay.

00:14:25.799 --> 00:14:26.764
But if we're gonna go that route,

00:14:26.793 --> 00:14:27.638
We'd better look the part.

00:14:34.016 --> 00:14:36.253
I look like one of the blues brothers.

00:14:36.572 --> 00:14:37.398
No, you don't.

00:14:37.886 --> 00:14:39.107
You look more like a...

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:40.854
Seventh-Grader at his first dance.

00:14:43.694 --> 00:14:44.896
I hate this thing.

00:14:44.933 --> 00:14:45.365
Hey.

00:14:45.741 --> 00:14:47.450
You want into that warehouse or not?

00:15:31.444 --> 00:15:32.158
What is that?

00:15:33.322 --> 00:15:34.487
It's an E.M.F. Meter...

00:15:34.937 --> 00:15:36.646
Reads electromagnetic frequencies.

00:15:37.437 --> 00:15:39.291
Yeah, I know what an E.M.F. Meter is,

00:15:39.309 --> 00:15:41.751
But why does that one look
like a busted-Up walkman?

00:15:42.804 --> 00:15:44.006
That's what I made it out of.

00:15:44.757 --> 00:15:45.714
It's homemade.

00:15:47.818 --> 00:15:49.677
Yeah, I can see that.

00:16:16.219 --> 00:16:17.778
Check out emergency door handle.

00:16:23.433 --> 00:16:24.372
What is this stuff?

00:16:24.503 --> 00:16:25.818
One way to find out.

00:16:38.681 --> 00:16:39.864
Homeland security?

00:16:40.697 --> 00:16:41.166
What?

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:42.706
One team of you guys isn't enough?

00:16:43.345 --> 00:16:44.190
What are you talking about?

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:46.539
Two of your buddies went
inside not five minutes ago.

00:17:26.927 --> 00:17:28.918
These monkey suits do come in handy.

00:17:30.439 --> 00:17:31.209
Listen Chuck

00:17:31.378 --> 00:17:32.429
It's like getting back on a horse,

00:17:32.977 --> 00:17:34.460
Only in this case, a little twin engine.

00:17:34.779 --> 00:17:35.606
Not even a horse

00:17:35.756 --> 00:17:36.545
More like a pony.

00:17:37.561 --> 00:17:38.481
I'll be right there with you too.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.490
Anytime you feel like you don't
want the wheel, I'll take over.

00:17:41.411 --> 00:17:42.218
Look, Chuck,

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:43.927
We don't have to do this today.

00:17:44.303 --> 00:17:45.110
I'm not trying to rush you.

00:17:46.032 --> 00:17:46.746
No, the...

00:17:47.854 --> 00:17:48.849
The waiting is worse.

00:17:51.328 --> 00:17:53.169
Okay, they're filling
up the tank. Then we go.

00:18:26.365 --> 00:18:26.928
Huh.

00:18:28.599 --> 00:18:30.045
This stuff is covered in sulfur.

00:18:30.327 --> 00:18:30.947
You're sure?

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:32.487
Take a look for yourself.

00:18:32.506 --> 00:18:33.876
"You effin' piece of..."

00:18:33.876 --> 00:18:35.210
If you fellows will excuse me,

00:18:35.247 --> 00:18:36.675
I have an idiot to fire.

00:18:43.603 --> 00:18:43.998
Hmm.

00:18:44.974 --> 00:18:47.754
Here is not too many things that
leave behind a sulfuric residue.

00:18:47.857 --> 00:18:48.833
Demonic possession?

00:18:49.378 --> 00:18:52.495
It would explain how a mortal man would have
the strength to open up an emergency hatch.

00:18:52.666 --> 00:18:54.074
If the guy was possessed,

00:18:54.318 --> 00:18:55.013
It's possible.

00:18:55.316 --> 00:18:57.701
This goes way beyond
floating over a bed or

00:18:57.720 --> 00:18:58.602
Barfing pea soup.

00:18:58.659 --> 00:19:00.180
What mean it's one thing
to possess a person,

00:19:00.217 --> 00:19:02.152
But to use them to take
down an entire airplane?

00:19:02.283 --> 00:19:03.992
You ever heard of
something like this before?

00:19:04.182 --> 00:19:04.707
Never.

00:19:10.623 --> 00:19:11.299
I'm ready.

00:19:11.506 --> 00:19:12.332
Let's do this.

00:19:20.588 --> 00:19:21.395
How you feeling?

00:19:21.658 --> 00:19:22.466
I feel great.

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:24.531
You'll be back flying
jumbos before you know it.

00:19:24.907 --> 00:19:25.752
I hope so.

00:19:29.472 --> 00:19:30.298
How long we been up?

00:19:30.862 --> 00:19:32.608
Huh... Almost 40 minutes.

00:19:32.965 --> 00:19:33.416
Wow.

00:19:33.773 --> 00:19:34.768
Time really does fly.

00:20:02.049 --> 00:20:02.669
So,

00:20:03.063 --> 00:20:05.166
Every religion in every world culture

00:20:05.223 --> 00:20:08.077
Has the concept of demons
and demonic possession, right?

00:20:08.426 --> 00:20:11.374
I mean christian, native
american, hindu. You name it.

00:20:11.468 --> 00:20:13.140
Yeah, but none of them
describe anything like this.

00:20:13.234 --> 00:20:14.360
Well, that's not exactly true.

00:20:14.398 --> 00:20:15.806
You see according to japanese beliefs,

00:20:15.844 --> 00:20:18.567
Certain demons are
behind certain disasters,

00:20:18.612 --> 00:20:19.476
Both natural

00:20:19.589 --> 00:20:20.453
And man-Made

00:20:20.509 --> 00:20:22.762
One causes earthquakes.
Another causes disease.

00:20:22.781 --> 00:20:24.340
And this one causes plane crashes?

00:20:28.607 --> 00:20:29.771
All right, so, what?

00:20:29.809 --> 00:20:31.837
We have a demonthat's
evolved with the times

00:20:31.875 --> 00:20:33.602
And found a way to
ratchet up the body count?

00:20:34.522 --> 00:20:35.106
Yeah.

00:20:36.252 --> 00:20:36.853
You know,

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:40.120
Who knows how many planes it's
brought down before this one?

00:20:45.026 --> 00:20:45.533
What?

00:20:47.091 --> 00:20:49.082
I don't know, man. This
isn't our normal gig.

00:20:49.645 --> 00:20:51.298
I mean, demons, they
don't want anything just

00:20:51.373 --> 00:20:53.251
Death and destructionfor its own sake.

00:20:54.246 --> 00:20:54.960
This is big.

00:20:56.389 --> 00:20:57.516
I wish dad was here.

00:20:58.587 --> 00:20:59.845
Yeah. Me too.

00:21:06.609 --> 00:21:06.984
Hello?

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:08.167
Dean it's Jerry

00:21:08.355 --> 00:21:09.069
Oh, hey, Jerry.

00:21:09.369 --> 00:21:10.327
My pilot friend...

00:21:12.318 --> 00:21:13.444
Chuck Lambert, is dead.

00:21:15.437 --> 00:21:15.925
Wha...

00:21:16.301 --> 00:21:17.446
Jerry, I'm sorry. What happened?

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:19.850
He and his buddy went
up in a small twin.

00:21:19.925 --> 00:21:20.939
About an hour ago.

00:21:21.578 --> 00:21:22.423
The plane went down.

00:21:22.799 --> 00:21:23.587
Where'd this happen?

00:21:23.907 --> 00:21:26.066
About 60 miles west
of here, near nazareth.

00:21:26.632 --> 00:21:28.078
I'll try to ignore the irony in that.

00:21:28.322 --> 00:21:28.885
I'm sorry?

00:21:29.130 --> 00:21:29.637
Nothing.

00:21:30.369 --> 00:21:32.303
Jerry hang in there, all right?
We'll catch up with you soon.

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:35.258
Another crash?

00:21:35.465 --> 00:21:35.990
Yeah.

00:21:36.366 --> 00:21:36.836
Let's go.

00:21:37.042 --> 00:21:37.587
Where?

00:21:38.282 --> 00:21:38.901
Nazareth.

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:51.792
Sulfur?

00:21:54.498 --> 00:21:55.681
Well, that's great.

00:21:56.414 --> 00:21:59.174
All right, that's two plane
crashes involving Chuck Lambert.

00:21:59.850 --> 00:22:01.278
This demon sounds likeit was after him.

00:22:01.684 --> 00:22:02.773
With all due respect to Chuck,

00:22:03.863 --> 00:22:05.966
If that's the case, that
would be the good news.

00:22:06.379 --> 00:22:07.186
What's the bad news?

00:22:07.374 --> 00:22:09.947
Chuck's plane went down
exactly 40 minutes into flight.

00:22:10.112 --> 00:22:10.995
And get this

00:22:11.145 --> 00:22:12.741
So did flight 2485.

00:22:13.042 --> 00:22:13.849
40 minutes?

00:22:14.262 --> 00:22:14.938
What does that mean?

00:22:15.521 --> 00:22:16.835
It's biblical numerology.

00:22:17.098 --> 00:22:19.089
You know Noah's ark,
it rained for 40days.

00:22:19.145 --> 00:22:20.122
The number means death.

00:22:20.518 --> 00:22:21.250
I went back,

00:22:21.325 --> 00:22:23.992
And there have been six plane
crashes over the last decade

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:26.809
That all went down
exactly 40 minutes in.

00:22:27.861 --> 00:22:28.743
Any survivors?

00:22:29.419 --> 00:22:29.889
No.

00:22:30.331 --> 00:22:30.856
Or not

00:22:30.932 --> 00:22:32.002
Until now,at least

00:22:32.021 --> 00:22:34.312
Not until flight 2485, for some reason.

00:22:35.363 --> 00:22:36.809
And the cockpit voice recorder

00:22:36.922 --> 00:22:38.180
Remember what the E.V.P. Said?

00:22:38.481 --> 00:22:39.345
"No survivors."

00:22:43.331 --> 00:22:44.702
It's going after all the survivors.

00:22:45.922 --> 00:22:47.012
Something finish the job.

00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:51.427
Really?

00:22:52.046 --> 00:22:53.812
Well, thank you for taking our survey,

00:22:53.830 --> 00:22:55.145
And if you do plan to fly,

00:22:55.164 --> 00:22:58.018
Please don't forget your friendsat
united britannia airlines.

00:22:58.751 --> 00:22:59.220
Thanks.

00:22:59.671 --> 00:23:00.309
All right.

00:23:00.424 --> 00:23:03.072
That takes care of Blaines
Anderson and Dennis Holloway.

00:23:03.186 --> 00:23:04.557
They're not flying anytime soon.

00:23:04.614 --> 00:23:07.149
So our only wildcard is the
flight attendant amanda walker.

00:23:07.412 --> 00:23:07.937
Right

00:23:07.975 --> 00:23:10.078
Her sister Karen said her flight
leaves Indianapolis at 8:00.

00:23:10.116 --> 00:23:11.675
Yeah but it's her first
night backon the job.

00:23:11.712 --> 00:23:13.064
That sounds like just our luck.

00:23:13.383 --> 00:23:14.998
Dean, this is a 5-Hour drive made

00:23:15.129 --> 00:23:16.575
Even with you behind the wheel.

00:23:17.159 --> 00:23:18.724
Call amanda's cellphone again,

00:23:18.742 --> 00:23:20.066
See if we can't head
her off at the pass.

00:23:20.121 --> 00:23:21.482
I already left her three voice messages.

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:23.587
She must have turned her cellphone off.

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:26.382
God,we're never gonna make it.

00:23:26.438 --> 00:23:27.127
We'll make it.

00:23:41.462 --> 00:23:42.096
Right there.

00:23:42.208 --> 00:23:43.326
They're boarding in 30 minutes.

00:23:43.475 --> 00:23:44.052
Okay.

00:23:44.593 --> 00:23:45.953
We still have some cards to play.

00:23:46.004 --> 00:23:46.992
We need to find a phone.

00:23:50.175 --> 00:23:51.107
Airport Services.

00:23:51.218 --> 00:23:52.299
Hi. Gate 13.

00:23:52.369 --> 00:23:53.524
<i>Who are you calling, Sir</i>

00:23:53.636 --> 00:23:55.253
I'm trying to contact an Amanda Walker.

00:23:55.275 --> 00:23:57.168
She's a flight attendant
on flight, um...

00:23:57.311 --> 00:23:58.588
Flight 424.

00:23:58.720 --> 00:23:59.755
<i>"Amanda walker,"</i>

00:24:00.019 --> 00:24:01.737
<i>"Amanda Walker, you have a phone call"</i>

00:24:01.825 --> 00:24:03.630
<i>"White courtesy phone, gate 13."</i>

00:24:06.569 --> 00:24:07.626
Come on.

00:24:09.233 --> 00:24:10.467
This is amanda walker.

00:24:10.841 --> 00:24:11.611
Miss walker.

00:24:12.052 --> 00:24:13.862
Hi, this is Dr. James Headfield

00:24:13.884 --> 00:24:16.064
From st. Francis memorial hospital.

00:24:16.394 --> 00:24:18.222
We have a Karen Walker here.

00:24:18.420 --> 00:24:19.125
Why Karen?

00:24:19.169 --> 00:24:21.282
Nothing serious just
a minor car accident,

00:24:21.317 --> 00:24:22.836
But she was injured, so

00:24:22.968 --> 00:24:25.962
Wa-Wait, that's impossible. I
just got off the phone with her.

00:24:29.227 --> 00:24:29.844
You what?

00:24:29.932 --> 00:24:30.790
Five minutes ago.

00:24:30.834 --> 00:24:33.499
She's at her house,
cramming for a final.

00:24:33.521 --> 00:24:34.467
Who is this?

00:24:35.668 --> 00:24:36.681
Uh, well...

00:24:37.099 --> 00:24:38.200
There must be some mistake.

00:24:38.222 --> 00:24:40.248
And how would you even know I was here?

00:24:41.987 --> 00:24:43.594
Is this one of Vince's friends?

00:24:45.243 --> 00:24:46.322
Guilty as charged.

00:24:47.136 --> 00:24:49.206
Wow. This is unbelievable.

00:24:50.065 --> 00:24:51.694
He's really sorry.

00:24:52.333 --> 00:24:53.918
Well, you tell him to
mind his own business

00:24:53.962 --> 00:24:55.723
And stay out of my life, okay?

00:24:55.811 --> 00:24:56.733
Yes, but...

00:24:57.085 --> 00:24:58.758
He really needs to see you tonight,

00:24:59.089 --> 00:24:59.815
So

00:24:59.925 --> 00:25:01.401
No, I'm sorry. It's too late.

00:25:01.599 --> 00:25:02.634
Don't be like that.

00:25:03.098 --> 00:25:04.199
Come on. The guy's

00:25:04.354 --> 00:25:05.983
A mess. Really. It's pathetic.

00:25:07.326 --> 00:25:08.009
Really?

00:25:08.229 --> 00:25:08.977
Oh, yeah.

00:25:09.638 --> 00:25:11.157
Look, I've got to go. Um...

00:25:11.168 --> 00:25:13.260
Tell him to call me when I land.

00:25:13.414 --> 00:25:15.176
No, no. Wait, Amanda. Amanda!

00:25:21.892 --> 00:25:22.817
How are you?

00:25:24.226 --> 00:25:25.393
Hey, boss. Hey

00:25:33.370 --> 00:25:34.272
Damn it!

00:25:34.779 --> 00:25:35.858
So close.

00:25:38.368 --> 00:25:40.063
All right, it's time for plan "B."

00:25:40.537 --> 00:25:41.594
We're getting on that plane.

00:25:41.704 --> 00:25:43.377
Oh,oh,Now, just hold on a second.

00:25:43.476 --> 00:25:44.092
Dean,

00:25:44.225 --> 00:25:45.392
That plane is leaving

00:25:45.436 --> 00:25:46.955
With over 100 passengers on board,

00:25:46.977 --> 00:25:47.902
And if we're right,

00:25:48.541 --> 00:25:49.840
That plane is gonna crash.

00:25:49.994 --> 00:25:50.632
I know.

00:25:50.743 --> 00:25:51.315
Okay.

00:25:51.408 --> 00:25:54.094
We're getting on the plane, we need
to find that demon and exorcise it.

00:25:54.138 --> 00:25:56.274
I'll get the tickets. You get
whatever you can out of the trunk.

00:25:56.318 --> 00:25:57.507
Whatever that will make
it through the security.

00:25:57.573 --> 00:25:58.872
Meet me back here in five minutes.

00:26:00.876 --> 00:26:01.889
Are you okay?

00:26:04.256 --> 00:26:05.533
No, not really.

00:26:06.810 --> 00:26:07.955
What? What's wrong?

00:26:10.124 --> 00:26:12.150
Well, I kind of have
this problem with, uh...

00:26:14.285 --> 00:26:15.100
Flying?

00:26:15.519 --> 00:26:17.236
It's never really been
an issue until now.

00:26:17.578 --> 00:26:18.436
You're joking, right?

00:26:18.502 --> 00:26:19.647
Do I look like I'm joking?

00:26:21.431 --> 00:26:23.016
Why do you think I
drive everywhere, sam?

00:26:24.139 --> 00:26:25.923
All right. Uh, I'll go.

00:26:26.212 --> 00:26:26.608
What?

00:26:26.630 --> 00:26:27.665
I'll do this oneon my own.

00:26:28.216 --> 00:26:29.008
Are you, nuts?

00:26:29.559 --> 00:26:30.924
You said that the plane's gonna crash.

00:26:30.968 --> 00:26:32.972
Dean, we can do it together,
or I can do this for myself.

00:26:33.016 --> 00:26:34.887
I'm not seeing a third option, here.

00:26:35.658 --> 00:26:36.583
Come on!

00:26:38.279 --> 00:26:38.962
Really?

00:26:41.274 --> 00:26:42.132
Man...

00:26:55.056 --> 00:26:57.015
Just try to relax. Just try to shut up.

00:27:26.878 --> 00:27:27.847
You're humming Metallica?

00:27:27.869 --> 00:27:29.014
Calms me down.

00:27:31.172 --> 00:27:32.031
Look, man,

00:27:32.405 --> 00:27:33.528
I get you're nervous, all right?

00:27:33.550 --> 00:27:35.113
But you got to stay focused.

00:27:36.452 --> 00:27:36.959
Okay.

00:27:36.981 --> 00:27:37.883
I mean, we got

00:27:37.994 --> 00:27:40.834
32 minutes and counting
to track this thing down

00:27:40.878 --> 00:27:44.159
Or who Everit's possessing, anyway
and perform a full-On exorcism.

00:27:44.181 --> 00:27:46.360
On a crowded plane.That's gonna be easy.

00:27:46.449 --> 00:27:48.078
Take it one step at a time, all right?

00:27:49.792 --> 00:27:50.540
Now,

00:27:50.662 --> 00:27:52.687
Who is it possessing?

00:27:53.766 --> 00:27:55.020
It's usually gonna be somebody

00:27:55.021 --> 00:27:56.078
With some sort of weakness, you know,

00:27:56.100 --> 00:27:58.214
A chink in the armor that
the demon can worm through,

00:27:58.621 --> 00:28:01.395
Somebody with an addiction
or emotional distress.

00:28:03.476 --> 00:28:04.071
Well,

00:28:04.269 --> 00:28:06.030
This is Amanda's first
flight after the crash.

00:28:06.074 --> 00:28:07.682
If I were her, I'd be pretty messed up.

00:28:07.748 --> 00:28:08.452
Mm-Hmm.

00:28:10.324 --> 00:28:11.204
Excuse me.

00:28:11.730 --> 00:28:12.479
Are you Amanda?

00:28:12.633 --> 00:28:13.470
No, I'm not.

00:28:13.514 --> 00:28:15.341
Oh, my mistake.

00:28:21.265 --> 00:28:23.313
All right, well, that's got
to be amanda back there,so

00:28:24.106 --> 00:28:25.162
I'll go talk to her,

00:28:25.295 --> 00:28:27.342
And, uh, I'll get a
read on her mental state.

00:28:27.783 --> 00:28:29.082
What if she's already possessed?

00:28:30.427 --> 00:28:31.880
There's ways to test that.

00:28:34.082 --> 00:28:35.337
I brought holy water.

00:28:36.218 --> 00:28:37.957
No. I think we can go more subtle.

00:28:38.424 --> 00:28:40.604
If she's possessed, she'll
flinch at the name of god.

00:28:41.176 --> 00:28:42.123
Oh. Nice.

00:28:44.259 --> 00:28:44.941
Hey.

00:28:45.107 --> 00:28:45.789
What?

00:28:45.965 --> 00:28:46.846
Say it in latin.

00:28:47.132 --> 00:28:47.793
I know.

00:28:47.881 --> 00:28:48.453
Okay.

00:28:48.696 --> 00:28:49.334
Hey!

00:28:49.841 --> 00:28:50.655
What?!

00:28:50.964 --> 00:28:52.791
Uh, in latin, it's "Cristo."

00:28:52.901 --> 00:28:54.707
Dude, I know! I'm not an idiot!

00:29:07.582 --> 00:29:08.705
Hi. Hi.

00:29:09.762 --> 00:29:10.841
Can I help you with something?

00:29:10.929 --> 00:29:11.832
Oh, no.

00:29:11.876 --> 00:29:13.835
I'm just a bit of an uneasy flier.

00:29:14.200 --> 00:29:15.851
It makes me feel better to
walk around a little bit.

00:29:15.961 --> 00:29:17.899
Oh, it happens to the best of us.

00:29:18.647 --> 00:29:21.686
Of course, you being a stewardess,
I guess flying comes easy to you.

00:29:22.820 --> 00:29:24.009
You'd be surprised.

00:29:24.339 --> 00:29:26.276
Really? You're a nervous flier?

00:29:26.959 --> 00:29:28.610
Yeah, maybe a little bit.

00:29:29.953 --> 00:29:31.605
How is it that,being a stewardess,

00:29:31.946 --> 00:29:33.025
You're scared to fly?

00:29:34.147 --> 00:29:35.381
Kind of a long story.

00:29:36.514 --> 00:29:38.100
Right. I'm sorry for asking.

00:29:38.177 --> 00:29:38.981
It's okay.

00:29:40.335 --> 00:29:41.942
You ever consider other employment?

00:29:43.219 --> 00:29:44.034
No.

00:29:44.562 --> 00:29:46.214
Look, everybody's scared of something.

00:29:46.269 --> 00:29:47.656
I just, uh...

00:29:48.449 --> 00:29:50.408
I'm not gonna let it hold me back.

00:29:51.685 --> 00:29:52.412
Huh.

00:29:53.436 --> 00:29:54.074
So...

00:29:56.893 --> 00:29:57.685
Cristo.

00:29:58.984 --> 00:30:00.305
I'm sorry. Did you say something?

00:30:05.547 --> 00:30:06.405
Cristo?

00:30:07.572 --> 00:30:08.783
I-I didn't, I didn't

00:30:09.818 --> 00:30:11.095
Yeah, nothing. Never mind.

00:30:15.296 --> 00:30:16.155
Okay.

00:30:24.100 --> 00:30:26.962
All right, well, she's got to be the
most well-Adjusted person on the planet.

00:30:27.006 --> 00:30:28.063
You said "cristo"? Yeah.

00:30:28.107 --> 00:30:29.439
And? There's no demon in her.

00:30:29.461 --> 00:30:31.024
There's no demon getting in her.

00:30:31.090 --> 00:30:32.874
So, if it's on the
plane, it can be anyone...

00:30:33.006 --> 00:30:34.063
Anywhere.

00:30:34.856 --> 00:30:37.035
Come on! That can't be normal! Hey, hey,

00:30:37.113 --> 00:30:39.447
It's just a little turbulence.

00:30:39.777 --> 00:30:41.340
Sam, this plane is going to crash, okay?

00:30:41.385 --> 00:30:42.838
So quit treating me
like I'm friggin' fool.

00:30:42.926 --> 00:30:44.709
You need to calm down.
No, I'm sorry I can't.

00:30:44.753 --> 00:30:46.063
Yes, you can.

00:30:46.459 --> 00:30:49.388
Dude, Stow the touchy-Feely,
self-Help yoga crap.

00:30:49.432 --> 00:30:50.489
It's not helping. Listen,
if you're panicked,

00:30:50.533 --> 00:30:51.744
You're wide opento demonic possession,

00:30:51.766 --> 00:30:53.836
So you need to calm yourself down

00:30:53.946 --> 00:30:54.936
Right now.

00:31:03.901 --> 00:31:04.694
Good.

00:31:05.971 --> 00:31:06.719
Now,

00:31:07.325 --> 00:31:09.659
I found an exorcism in here
that I think is gonna work

00:31:10.254 --> 00:31:11.487
The ritual romano.

00:31:12.544 --> 00:31:13.424
What do we have to do?

00:31:13.887 --> 00:31:14.680
It's two parts.

00:31:14.724 --> 00:31:17.146
The first part expels the
demon from the victim's body.

00:31:17.301 --> 00:31:20.405
It makes it manifest, which
actually makes it more powerful.

00:31:20.680 --> 00:31:21.451
More powerful?

00:31:21.561 --> 00:31:22.463
Yeah. How?

00:31:23.146 --> 00:31:24.599
Well, it doesn't need to
possess someone anymore.

00:31:24.643 --> 00:31:26.471
It can just wreak havoc on its own.

00:31:26.735 --> 00:31:28.298
Oh. And why is that a good thing?

00:31:28.827 --> 00:31:30.808
Well, because the second part

00:31:31.689 --> 00:31:33.164
Sends the bastard back to hell

00:31:33.561 --> 00:31:34.728
Once and for all.

00:31:36.247 --> 00:31:37.942
First thing's first we got to find it.

00:32:15.491 --> 00:32:16.423
Ohh! Don't do that.

00:32:16.531 --> 00:32:17.333
Anything?

00:32:17.527 --> 00:32:19.390
No, nothing. How much time we got?

00:32:19.650 --> 00:32:20.538
15 minutes.

00:32:21.795 --> 00:32:23.116
Maybe we missed somebody.

00:32:23.874 --> 00:32:25.390
Maybe the thing's just not on the plane.

00:32:26.660 --> 00:32:27.613
You believe that?

00:32:28.371 --> 00:32:29.454
Well, I will if you will.

00:32:38.958 --> 00:32:39.933
What? What is it?

00:32:41.255 --> 00:32:41.969
Cristo.

00:32:57.116 --> 00:32:58.286
She's not gonna believe this.

00:32:58.437 --> 00:32:59.476
12 minutes, dude.

00:33:01.890 --> 00:33:02.735
Oh, hi.

00:33:03.491 --> 00:33:05.084
Flight's not too bumpy for you, I hope.

00:33:05.157 --> 00:33:07.330
Actually, that's kind of what
we need to talk to you about.

00:33:07.547 --> 00:33:09.430
Um, okay.What can I do for you?

00:33:09.913 --> 00:33:11.507
This is gonna sound nuts, but

00:33:11.871 --> 00:33:14.165
We just don't have time for the whole
"the true this out there" speech right now.

00:33:14.213 --> 00:33:16.362
Look, we know you were on flight 2485.

00:33:18.098 --> 00:33:19.040
Who are you guys?

00:33:19.160 --> 00:33:21.309
Now, we've spoken to
some other survivors.

00:33:21.430 --> 00:33:23.820
We know something brought down that
plane and it wasn't a mechanical failure.

00:33:23.893 --> 00:33:24.907
We need your help

00:33:24.979 --> 00:33:26.694
Because we need to stop
from happening again.

00:33:26.814 --> 00:33:27.716
Here. Now. I'm sorry

00:33:27.788 --> 00:33:30.638
Here. I-I'm very busy. Whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa. Wait a second.

00:33:30.710 --> 00:33:32.110
I'm not gonna hurt you, okay?

00:33:32.255 --> 00:33:33.631
But listen to me, huh...

00:33:33.752 --> 00:33:36.039
The pilot in 2485, Chuck Lambert.

00:33:36.160 --> 00:33:37.029
He's dead.

00:33:37.712 --> 00:33:38.750
Wait. What?

00:33:38.919 --> 00:33:40.126
What, Chuck is dead?

00:33:40.416 --> 00:33:41.961
He died in a plane crash.

00:33:42.106 --> 00:33:43.652
That's two plane crashes in two months.

00:33:43.676 --> 00:33:45.318
That doesn't strike you as strange?

00:33:46.066 --> 00:33:47.853
Look, there was
something wrong with 2485.

00:33:47.878 --> 00:33:49.203
Now maybe you're
sensitive maybe you didn't

00:33:49.228 --> 00:33:50.628
But there's something
wrong with this flight, too.

00:33:50.653 --> 00:33:52.303
Amanda,you have to believe us.

00:33:57.609 --> 00:33:58.534
On...

00:33:59.484 --> 00:34:01.209
On 2485,

00:34:01.259 --> 00:34:03.059
There was this man.

00:34:03.109 --> 00:34:05.234
He...had these eyes.

00:34:05.509 --> 00:34:07.162
Yes. That's exactly
what we're talking about.

00:34:07.184 --> 00:34:08.837
I don't understand what
are you asking me to do?

00:34:08.859 --> 00:34:10.648
Okay. The copilot, we need
you bring him back here.

00:34:10.693 --> 00:34:12.754
Why? What does he have
to do with anything?

00:34:12.821 --> 00:34:13.750
Don't have time to explain.

00:34:13.772 --> 00:34:15.199
We just need to talk to him. Okay?

00:34:15.312 --> 00:34:16.693
How am I supposed to go in the cockpit

00:34:16.738 --> 00:34:18.572
And get the copilot--
Do whatever it takes

00:34:18.617 --> 00:34:20.293
Tell him there's
something broken back here,

00:34:20.338 --> 00:34:21.719
Whatever will get him
out of that cockpit.

00:34:21.787 --> 00:34:23.213
Do you know that I could lose my job

00:34:23.236 --> 00:34:25.410
If you -- You're gonna lose a
lot more if you don't help us out.

00:34:32.008 --> 00:34:32.755
Okay.

00:35:12.834 --> 00:35:13.989
Yeah, what's the problem?

00:35:20.170 --> 00:35:22.841
Wait. What are you doing? You said
you were just gonna talk to him.

00:35:22.887 --> 00:35:24.358
We are gonna talk to him.

00:35:33.397 --> 00:35:34.718
Oh, my god.What's wrong with him?

00:35:34.784 --> 00:35:35.709
Look. We need you calm.

00:35:35.753 --> 00:35:37.537
We need you outside the curtain.
Well, I don't underst..., I don't know

00:35:37.581 --> 00:35:39.166
Don't let anybody in,
okay? Can you do that?

00:35:39.210 --> 00:35:40.487
Can you do that?

00:35:40.795 --> 00:35:41.380
Amanda?

00:35:41.623 --> 00:35:42.177
Okay.

00:35:42.907 --> 00:35:43.483
Okay.

00:35:45.161 --> 00:35:47.331
Hurry up, sam. I don't know
how much longer I can hold him.

00:36:09.248 --> 00:36:10.842
I know what happened to your girlfriend!

00:36:12.768 --> 00:36:14.318
She must have died screaming!

00:36:15.004 --> 00:36:16.642
Even now, she's burning!

00:36:19.551 --> 00:36:20.260
Sam!

00:36:23.865 --> 00:36:25.038
"Prayer"...

00:36:27.761 --> 00:36:28.470
I got him.

00:36:49.398 --> 00:36:50.018
Where'd he go?

00:36:50.085 --> 00:36:50.992
He's in the plane.

00:36:51.059 --> 00:36:52.564
Hurry up.We got to finish it.

00:38:39.895 --> 00:38:40.426
I don't know.

00:38:40.515 --> 00:38:41.733
I was walking through the airport,

00:38:41.976 --> 00:38:43.283
Then it all goes blank.

00:38:43.570 --> 00:38:45.740
I don't even remember
getting on the plane.

00:38:47.751 --> 00:38:48.902
Anything else?

00:38:49.279 --> 00:38:50.186
No, that's all.

00:38:53.968 --> 00:38:54.920
"Thank you"

00:39:01.318 --> 00:39:02.337
Let's get out of here.

00:39:05.281 --> 00:39:06.123
You okay?

00:39:07.827 --> 00:39:08.580
Dean,

00:39:10.550 --> 00:39:12.166
It knew about Jessica.

00:39:14.841 --> 00:39:17.210
Sam, these things,t-They read minds.

00:39:17.586 --> 00:39:18.317
They lie.

00:39:19.091 --> 00:39:20.309
All right?That's all it was.

00:39:21.992 --> 00:39:22.612
Yeah.

00:39:25.054 --> 00:39:25.829
Come on.

00:39:32.028 --> 00:39:34.370
Nobody knows what you
guys did, but i do.

00:39:35.787 --> 00:39:37.470
A lot of people could have been killed.

00:39:38.931 --> 00:39:40.277
Your dad's gonna be real proud.

00:39:40.808 --> 00:39:42.137
We'll see you around, Jerry.

00:39:45.369 --> 00:39:46.344
You know, Jerry.

00:39:46.676 --> 00:39:47.251
Yeah.

00:39:47.867 --> 00:39:50.480
I meant to ask you how did you
get my cellphone number, anyway?

00:39:50.524 --> 00:39:52.162
I've only had it for like six months.

00:39:52.428 --> 00:39:53.624
Your dad gave it to me.

00:39:54.266 --> 00:39:54.704
What?

00:39:54.749 --> 00:39:56.077
When did you talk to him?

00:39:56.254 --> 00:39:58.690
I mean, I didn't exactly talk to him,but

00:39:59.110 --> 00:40:01.767
I called his number. His voice
message said to give you a call.

00:40:03.711 --> 00:40:04.508
Thanks again, guys.

00:40:21.400 --> 00:40:22.884
This doesn't make any sense, man.

00:40:22.906 --> 00:40:25.054
I've called dad's number like 50 times.

00:40:25.077 --> 00:40:26.383
It's been out of service.

00:40:27.706 --> 00:40:28.902
This is John Winchester.

00:40:29.234 --> 00:40:30.540
I can't be reached.

00:40:30.549 --> 00:40:32.896
If this is an emergency,
call my son, Dean

00:40:33.848 --> 00:40:38.648

866-907-3235

00:40:39.644 --> 00:40:40.729
He'll can help.



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
